@page "/components/datagrid/editing"

<DocsPage>
    <DocsPageHeader Title="DataGrid - Editing" Component="@nameof(VekDataGrid<T>)">
        <Description>
            Learn about DataGrid editing capabilities, including form/dialog editing, inline row editing, custom editors, and validation integration.
        </Description>
    </DocsPageHeader>
    <DocsPageContent>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Editing">
                <Description>
                    Enable editing with <CodeInline>ReadOnly="false"</CodeInline>. Use <CodeInline>DataGridEditMode.Form</CodeInline> for dialog editing, <CodeInline>DataGridEditMode.Cell</CodeInline> for always-on cell editing, or <CodeInline>DataGridEditMode.Inline</CodeInline> for single-row inline editing triggered manually.
                    <br /><br />

                    Edit events:
                    <ul>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>StartedEditingItem</CodeInline>: editing begins</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>FormFieldChanged</CodeInline>: a field changes in form mode</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>CommittedItemChanges</CodeInline>: runs before applying changes</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>CommittedItemChanged</CodeInline>: runs after a successful commit</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>CanceledEditingItem</CodeInline>: editing is canceled</li>
                    </ul>

                    In form mode, <CodeInline>CommittedItemChanges</CodeInline> receives the edited copy and returns <CodeInline>Close</CodeInline> to save or <CodeInline>KeepOpen</CodeInline> to keep the dialog open. In this example, a negative Molar mass keeps the form open.
                    <br /><br />

                    Set <CodeInline>Editable</CodeInline> to <CodeInline>false</CodeInline> to disable editing for a column. Set <CodeInline>Required</CodeInline> to <CodeInline>false</CodeInline> to make a field optional.
                    <br /><br />

                    Editable cells use a matching input by default. Use an <CodeInline Tag>EditTemplate</CodeInline> for custom editors. In cell mode, standard columns commit automatically, but controls inside an <CodeInline Tag>EditTemplate</CodeInline> must handle commits in their value-changed callback.
                    <br /><br />

                    To add and edit a new row programmatically, call <CodeInline>SetEditingItemAsync</CodeInline> with a new <CodeInline>T</CodeInline> instance in form mode. In cell mode, add the new item directly to <CodeInline>Items</CodeInline>.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridEditingExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                <DataGridEditingExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Inline Row Editing">
                <Description>
                    Use <CodeInline>DataGridEditMode.Inline</CodeInline> for single-row inline editing. This mode combines the best of form and cell editing:
                    <ul>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span>Only one row can be edited at a time</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span>Editing is triggered manually via an Edit button (not by clicking cells)</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span>Edit controls appear inline within the row's cells</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span>All other rows remain read-only while one is being edited</li>
                    </ul>
                    <br />
                    Use <CodeInline>EditTemplate</CodeInline> to define custom editors for each column. The <CodeInline>CellContext</CodeInline> provides:
                    <ul>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>IsEditing</CodeInline>: indicates if the current row is being edited</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>Item</CodeInline>: the editing copy when in edit mode, or the source item otherwise</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>Actions.StartEditingItemAsync</CodeInline>: begins editing the row</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>Actions.CommitEditingItemAsync</CodeInline>: saves changes and exits edit mode</li>
                        <li><span class="mr-2">&bull;</span><CodeInline>Actions.CancelEditingItemAsync</CodeInline>: discards changes and exits edit mode</li>
                    </ul>
                    <br />
                    The row's editors are validated before a commit is applied, so a failing <CodeInline>Required</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>Validation</CodeInline> rule keeps the row in edit mode on its own. For checks the editors cannot express, such as uniqueness or a server round-trip, validate in <CodeInline>CommittedItemChanges</CodeInline> and return <CodeInline>KeepOpen</CodeInline>.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridInlineRowEditingExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                <DataGridInlineRowEditingExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Validator">
                <Description>
                    When a <CodeInline>&lt;VekDataGrid></CodeInline> is used as part of a <CodeInline>VekForm</CodeInline> you might want to
                    bind the <CodeInline>Validator</CodeInline> property to the outer <CodeInline>VekForm</CodeInline> so that validation
                    and <CodeInline>IsTouched</CodeInline> states are reflected in/propagated to the outer <CodeInline>VekForm</CodeInline>.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent DarkenBackground="true" Code="@nameof(DataGridValidatorExample)" ShowCode="false" Block="true" FullWidth="true">
                <DataGridValidatorExample />
            </SectionContent>
        </DocsPageSection>

    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>